# Logstash pipeline check

Run the script from the repository root:

```bash
export ELASTICSEARCH_URL="https://elasticsearch:9200"
export ELASTICSEARCH_USERNAME="elastic"
export ELASTICSEARCH_PASSWORD="password"

./references/scripts/check-logstash-pipelines.py \
  "minion-*-partial-* minion-*-sold-* nr-* nre-* birl-*" \
  "test-* tester-* mule-* magecart-* maid-* minion-*-account-* minion-*-full-* minion-*-cpp-* dome-*"
```

The two pattern strings are the `pipeline_id` values for `logstash-1` and
`logstash-2` in `prod-red.tfvars.json`:

```text
Settings.clusters.production.red.logstash.logstash-1.pipeline_id
Settings.clusters.production.red.logstash.logstash-2.pipeline_id
```

Copy the complete value inside quotes after each `pipeline_id`. The script gets
all pipeline names from Elasticsearch and reports any name that does not match
either pattern string.
